From f4527edb07aaa082f9ad4c14222a38c4c07112a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:51:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update-pause): alarm key names the host; link
 sibling hosts' open alarms for one refusal

Every worker shares the install root and the gateway unit, so every worker's
update-pause alarm had one idempotency key (update-pause-deferred:156199e9...).
On 2026-11-12 worker-5, worker-1 and worker-6 each filed a card for one
fleet-wide refusal; three owners investigated from scratch and two opened
competing PRs (#1554, #1564).

- the key is sha256(host, install root, unit); an open card of this host under
  the pre-host key is still kept
- before filing, look board-wide (live file, then Board replica) for an open
  alarm for the same unit and refusal class on another host; the new card names
  it as the likely shared cause and parks on its fix first
- the sibling hears of this host (host, time, refusal line): directly when the
  card is writable here, else from its home on its next deferral

Card: t_01a1d0a5affda05c
---
